cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the code, lifetime data, or computational results in this
  repository, please cite this software archive. Cite the associated
  journal article separately when its bibliographic record is available.
type: software
title: >-
  Regime-Aware Censored Weibull Reliability Inference for Small-Sample
  Optocoupler Thermal-Cycling Data: Computational Reproducibility Archive
authors:
  - family-names: "Bhattacharyya"
    given-names: "Anindya"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Anindya001/OPTO_TREL_SUB_R3_11_11_2026"
url: "https://github.com/Anindya001/OPTO_TREL_SUB_R3_11_11_2026"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility archive accompanying IEEE Transactions on Reliability
  manuscript TR-2026-412.R3. It contains unit-level right-censored thermal
  cycling lifetimes for 48 optocouplers, Weibull accelerated-life inference,
  posterior draws, comparator analyses, statistical checks, and computational
  figure-generation scripts. Experimental apparatus imagery, raw electrical
  traces, and X-ray photographs are outside the archive's scope.
keywords:
  - optocoupler
  - thermal cycling
  - reliability
  - right censoring
  - Weibull model
  - Bayesian inference
  - reproducible research
